{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' openspec/changes/skill-decomposition/proposal.md\"","aggregated_output":"## Why\n\nDarkfactory's skills are scattered across three locations, require two repo clones and 8+ manual symlinks to install, and include duplicate files. External skills are forked copies we can't improve. There are no standalone skills for adversarial review, codex dispatch, or OpenSpec planning outside a mission.\n\n## What Changes\n\n- Move all skills from .claude/skills/ to skills/ at repo root\n- Fork 6 external skills (grill-me, write-a-prd, ubiquitous-language, tdd, test-quality-review, security-review) into the repo\n- Create 2 new standalone skills: /adversarial, /dispatch\n- Create install.sh that symlinks skills to ~/.claude/skills/\n- Delete .codex/skills/ duplicates\n- Simplify /mission-init to verify symlinks instead of checking multiple locations\n- Update README with 3-command install\n\n## Capabilities\n\n### New Capabilities\n\n- `adversarial-review`: Dual-agent (Claude + Codex) parallel code review as a standalone skill\n- `dispatch-skill`: Skill wrapper for the darkfactory-dispatch binary\n- `install-script`: One-command skill installation via install.sh\n\n### Modified Capabilities\n\n- `setup-verification`: mission-init simplified to verify symlinks and CLI tools\n- `skill-layout`: All skills moved from .claude/skills/ to skills/ at repo root\n\n## Impact\n\n- New directory: skills/ (12 skill directories)\n- New file: install.sh\n- Modified: README.md (install instructions)\n- No changes to tools/darkfactory-dispatch/ or openspec/\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"tool_end","dispatch_id":"01KQ7GQ976BYM3RDS75E2VS1QQ","ts":"2026-04-27T13:06:06Z","tool":"command_execution"}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' openspec/changes/skill-decomposition/design.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Design: skill-decomposition\n\n## Final directory state\n\n```\n~/.darkfactory/\n  skills/\n    adversarial/SKILL.md        # New — standalone dual-agent review\n    dispatch/SKILL.md           # New — user-facing darkfactory-dispatch wrapper\n    grill/SKILL.md              # Forked from grill-me (name change only)\n    language/SKILL.md           # Forked from ubiquitous-language (name change only)\n    mission/\n      SKILL.md                  # Moved from .claude/skills/mission/ (unchanged)\n      templates/                # Moved unchanged\n      prompts/                  # Moved, scrutiny-validator.md gets 1 ref update\n    mission-init/SKILL.md       # Renamed from darkfactory-init + rewritten\n    mission-resume/SKILL.md     # Moved from .claude/skills/mission-resume/ (unchanged)\n    mission-status/SKILL.md     # Moved from .claude/skills/mission-status/ (unchanged)\n    prd/SKILL.md                # Forked from write-a-prd (name change only)\n    security/SKILL.md           # Forked from security-review (strip toyo sections)\n    tdd/\n      SKILL.md                # Forked from tdd (name change only)\n      deep-modules.md         # Forked unchanged\n      interface-design.md     # Forked unchanged\n      mocking.md              # Forked unchanged\n      refactoring.md          # Forked unchanged\n      tests.md                # Forked unchanged\n    test-quality/SKILL.md     # Forked from test-quality-review (name change only)\n  install.sh                  # New — symlinks skills/ to ~/.claude/skills/\n  tools/darkfactory-dispatch/ # Unchanged\n  docs/                       # Unchanged\n  openspec/                   # Unchanged\n  README.md                   # Rewritten: new install, new skill names, owned skills\n  UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md      # Minor: \"separate skill\" → \"owned skill\" for test-quality\n```\n\n**Deleted:**\n- `.claude/skills/` — entire directory\n- `.codex/skills/` — entire directory (duplicates)\n\n## Key decisions\n\n**skills/ at repo root, not .claude/skills/**\nInstall.sh manages one symlink per skill from `~/.claude/skills/<name>` → `~/.darkfactory/skills/<name>`. This separates what's owned from how Claude Code discovers it. The `.claude/` directory inside the repo becomes empty and can be removed.\n\n**Naming convention**\nForked and new skills use bare names (no prefix): `grill`, `language`, `prd`, `tdd`, `test-quality`, `security`, `adversarial`, `dispatch`. The three mission utility skills keep their `mission-` prefix (`mission-resume`, `mission-status`, `mission-init`) since that prefix is part of their established identity and changing it would break existing workflows.\n\n**Fork, don't symlink external skills**\nExternal symlinks (to `~/.darkfactory-skills/`) meant we couldn't improve skills without touching a second repo and they were silently out of date. Forking makes this repo self-contained. The external `layercodedev/skills` repo dependency is eliminated entirely.\n\n**test-quality is a name-only fork**\nThe `test-quality-review` skill has no toyo-specific content to strip. The only change is the frontmatter name field. Content is preserved exactly.\n\n**security strips toyo sections only**\nThe `security-review` skill has toyo-specific sections (references to toyo's review conventions and severity levels). These are removed. The general security review logic is preserved.\n\n**adversarial is written fresh, not forked**\nThe existing adversarial reviewer logic lives in `mission/prompts/adversarial-reviewer.md` (used only by mission Phase 9). The new `/adversarial` standalone skill embeds its own reviewer instructions. Mission Phase 9 continues to use `prompts/adversarial-reviewer.md` unchanged — the mission-orchestration spec prohibits behavior changes to mission.\n\n**dispatch is a thin skill**\n`/dispatch` wraps `darkfactory-dispatch` with a human-readable interface. It handles prompt file creation, JSON result parsing, and error surfacing. It does not add retry logic or state management — those are handled by the binary.\n\n**mission-init checks symlinks, not source locations**\nOld `darkfactory-init` checked two possible install locations (`.claude/skills/` inside the repo and `~/.darkfactory-skills/`). After this refactor, there is exactly one install path: `install.sh`. The new `/mission-init` verifies that `~/.claude/skills/<name>` is a symlink resolving to `~/.darkfactory/skills/<name>` for each of the 12 skills. If broken or missing, it points to `install.sh`.\n\n## Module concerns\n\nEach skill is a self-contained module. Its public interface is the frontmatter (name, description, user-invokable). Its hidden implementation is the SKILL.md body. No skill file imports from another at the filesystem level.\n\nThe mission skill is intentionally monolithic (one SKILL.md, ~825 lines). Per spec, it is not decomposed into sub-skills. Its companion files (templates/, prompts/) are read on demand and remain nested under `skills/mission/`.\n\n## Reference updates required\n\nTwo files need content changes beyond a move or name change:\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `skills/mission/SKILL.md` | `/grill-me` → `/grill`, `/write-a-prd` → `/prd`, `/ubiquitous-language` → `/language`, `/darkfactory-init` → `/mission-init` (all occurrences) |\n| `skills/mission/prompts/scrutiny-validator.md` | `/test-quality-review` → `/test-quality` (check 14) |\n\nThe SKILL.md ref update was added during the coverage audit to implement PRD user story 10. All four old skill names appear in the SKILL.md body where the mission orchestrator invokes sub-skills. After Task 1a, those references resolve to the new bare names installed via `install.sh`.\n\n## install.sh design\n\n```sh\n#!/bin/sh\nDARKFACTORY=\"$HOME/.darkfactory\"\nSKILLS_DIR=\"$DARKFACTORY/skills\"\nCLAUDE_SKILLS=\"$HOME/.claude/skills\"\n\nmkdir -p \"$CLAUDE_SKILLS\"\n\nfor skill_dir in \"$SKILLS_DIR\"/*/; do\n    name=$(basename \"$skill_dir\")\n    target=\"$CLAUDE_SKILLS/$name\"\n    ln -sf \"$skill_dir\" \"$target\"\n    echo \"linked: $target -> $skill_dir\"\ndone\n\necho \"Done. $(ls \"$SKILLS_DIR\" | wc -l | tr -d ' ') skills installed.\"\n```\n\n- `#!/bin/sh` not `#!/bin/bash` — POSIX portable\n- `ln -sf` — creates or overwrites; idempotent\n- Loops over `skills/*/` — adding a new skill directory automatically gets picked up on next run without editing the script\n- Does not touch any existing `~/.claude/skills/` entry that isn't a Darkfactory skill\n\n## README rewrite scope\n\nThree sections change:\n\n1. **Setup / First-time install** — replace the block of 4 manual `ln -sf` commands with:\n   ```bash\n   git clone https://github.com/layercodedev/darkfactory.git ~/.darkfactory\n   ~/.darkfactory/install.sh\n   ```\n\n2. **Skills table** — replace the 4-row table (mission, mission-resume, mission-status, darkfactory-init) with the full 12-skill table.\n\n3. **Required external skills** — this table listed 6 skills from `layercodedev/skills`. After the refactor, all are owned. Replace the section with a brief note that `/review` and `/simplify` are built-in Claude Code skills (always available), and `/test-app` and `/demo-video` are optional project-specific skills the user writes themselves.\n\n## Task order\n\nTasks decompose naturally into these groups:\n\n1. **Move existing skills** — mission (+ templates/ prompts/), mission-resume, mission-status\n2. **Fork external skills** — grill, language, prd, tdd (+ companions), test-quality (+ scrutiny-validator.md ref update), security\n3. **Rewrite init**\n4. **Write new skills** — adversarial, dispatch\n5. **Create install.sh**\n6. **Update README.md and UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md**\n7. **Closing tasks** — smoke test, cleanup, module shape re-check, docs\n\nGroups 1–2 are the bulk of the file work and are low-risk (move/copy with name changes). Groups 3–4 are the only net-new writing. Groups 5–6 are targeted edits. Each group maps cleanly to one or two tasks.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"tool_end","dispatch_id":"01KQ7GQ976BYM3RDS75E2VS1QQ","ts":"2026-04-27T13:06:06Z","tool":"command_execution"}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' openspec/changes/skill-decomposition/tasks.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Tasks: skill-decomposition\n\n## Feature Tasks\n\n- [x] 1. Move mission skill, mission-resume, and mission-status\n  Move `.claude/skills/mission/` (SKILL.md + templates/ + prompts/) to `skills/mission/`. Move `.claude/skills/mission-resume/` to `skills/mission-resume/`. Move `.claude/skills/mission-status/` to `skills/mission-status/`. Do not change any skill content in any of these three.\n\n- [x] 1a. Update mission SKILL.md skill references\n  In `skills/mission/SKILL.md`, replace all occurrences of old skill invocation names with new ones: `/grill-me` → `/grill`, `/write-a-prd` → `/prd`, `/ubiquitous-language` → `/language`, `/darkfactory-init` → `/mission-init`. No other content changes. This implements PRD user story 10 and was added during the coverage audit.\n\n- [ ] 2. Fork grill, language, and prd skills\n  Copy `~/.darkfactory-skills/grill-me/SKILL.md` to `skills/grill/SKILL.md`, update frontmatter name to `grill`. Copy `~/.darkfactory-skills/ubiquitous-language/SKILL.md` to `skills/language/SKILL.md`, update frontmatter name to `language`. Copy `~/.darkfactory-skills/write-a-prd/SKILL.md` to `skills/prd/SKILL.md`, update frontmatter name to `prd`. Content otherwise unchanged.\n\n- [ ] 3. Fork tdd and test-quality skills\n  Copy `~/.darkfactory-skills/tdd/SKILL.md` and all 5 companion files (`deep-modules.md`, `interface-design.md`, `mocking.md`, `refactoring.md`, `tests.md`) to `skills/tdd/`, update frontmatter name to `tdd`. Copy `~/.darkfactory-skills/test-quality-review/SKILL.md` to `skills/test-quality/SKILL.md`, update frontmatter name to `test-quality`. Also update the one reference in `skills/mission/prompts/scrutiny-validator.md`: replace `/test-quality-review` with `/test-quality` in check 14.\n\n- [ ] 4. Fork security skill\n  Copy `~/.darkfactory-skills/security-review/SKILL.md` to `skills/security/SKILL.md`. Update frontmatter name to `security`. Remove any toyo-review-specific sections (references to toyo's review conventions or toyo-specific severity levels). Preserve all general security review logic.\n\n- [ ] 5. Write mission-init skill\n  Write `skills/mission-init/SKILL.md`. This replaces `darkfactory-init` with symlink-based verification. The skill checks that each of the 12 skills has a symlink at `~/.claude/skills/<name>` pointing to `~/.darkfactory/skills/<name>`. On missing or broken symlinks it suggests running `install.sh`. Retains: CLI tool checks (codex, darkfactory-dispatch, gh, openspec, jq), coverage tool detection per project language (Rust/TypeScript/Python), and `openspec init --tools claude,codex --force` if `openspec/config.yaml` is absent.\n\n- [ ] 6. Write adversarial skill\n  Write `skills/adversarial/SKILL.md`. Standalone dual-agent review skill: dispatches a Codex reviewer via `darkfactory-dispatch --async`, then launches a Claude reviewer via the Agent tool. Both receive identical input (current diff by default; PR diff via `gh pr diff <number>` if a PR number is given; a specific file if a path is given). Reports written to `mission/validations/adversarial-codex.md` and `adversarial-claude.md` (or temp paths outside a mission). After both complete, surfaces disagreements between the two reports.\n\n- [ ] 7. Write dispatch skill\n  Write `skills/dispatch/SKILL.md`. Thin user-facing wrapper around the `darkfactory-dispatch` binary. Accepts a task description inline or prompts for one. Calls `darkfactory-dispatch` with a prompt file and `--json`, parses the structured result, and presents outcome (status, duration, files written, output path). Reports failure clearly; does not suppress it.\n\n- [ ] 8. Create install.sh\n  Write `install.sh` at the repo root. POSIX-portable (`#!/bin/sh`), loops over `skills/*/` directories, creates `ln -sf` symlinks from `~/.claude/skills/<name>` to `~/.darkfactory/skills/<name>` for each. Idempotent. Prints one line per skill and a final count. Make the file executable.\n\n- [ ] 9. Update README.md and UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md\n  Rewrite three README sections: (1) First-time install — replace the block of manual `ln -sf` commands with `git clone` + `~/.darkfactory/install.sh`. (2) Skills table — replace the 4-row legacy table with the full 12-skill table. (3) Required external skills section — skills previously listed as external (`grill-me`, `ubiquitous-language`, `write-a-prd`, `tdd`, `test-quality-review`, `security-review`) are now bundled; remove them from the external table, keep only `/review` and `/simplify` (built-in Claude Code) and `/test-app` and `/demo-video` (optional project-specific). Update UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md: change \"separate skill\" to \"owned skill\" in the test-quality term definition.\n\n## Closing Tasks\n\n- [ ] C1. Smoke test\n  Run `~/.darkfactory/install.sh` and verify: (1) all 12 symlinks exist under `~/.claude/skills/` and resolve to the correct `~/.darkfactory/skills/<name>` targets; (2) running `/mission-init` in a project with a `Cargo.toml`, `package.json`, or `pyproject.toml` reports the expected coverage tool status.\n\n- [ ] C2. Cleanup\n  Remove any dead code, leftover scaffold, or draft files introduced during the mission. Check that no skill file contains references to old names (`grill-me`, `write-a-prd`, `ubiquitous-language`, `darkfactory-init`, `test-quality-review`). Verify no skill references the external `~/.darkfactory-skills/` repo path.\n\n- [ ] C3. Module shape re-check\n  Audit the final `skills/` directory against `design.md`. Verify the 12 skill directories exist with correct names, each has a `SKILL.md` with valid frontmatter, `skills/mission/` has `templates/` and `prompts/` subdirectories with all original files, and `skills/tdd/` has all 5 companion files. Flag any drift from the design.\n\n- [ ] C4. Documentation\n  Verify `README.md` accurately describes the post-refactor install and skill set. Verify `UBIQUITOUS_LANGUAGE.md` no longer describes test-quality as a \"separate skill\". Update any other in-repo documentation that references the old skill names or old install process.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
