{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' openspec/changes/skill-decomposition/specs/adversarial-review/spec.md\"","aggregated_output":"## ADDED Requirements\n\n### Requirement: /adversarial skill exists\nA skill named `adversarial` SHALL exist at `skills/adversarial/SKILL.md` and be user-invokable.\n\n#### Scenario: Skill metadata is correct\n- **WHEN** inspecting `skills/adversarial/SKILL.md`\n- **THEN** the frontmatter `name` is `adversarial`\n- **AND** `user-invokable` is `true`\n- **AND** the description mentions dual-agent review and Claude + Codex\n\n### Requirement: /adversarial accepts a review target\nThe skill SHALL accept an optional argument specifying what to review: a PR number, a file path, or no argument (defaults to current diff).\n\n#### Scenario: No argument reviews current diff\n- **WHEN** `/adversarial` is invoked with no arguments\n- **THEN** the skill reviews uncommitted changes (`git diff` + `git diff --staged`)\n\n#### Scenario: PR number argument reviews PR diff\n- **WHEN** `/adversarial <number>` is invoked with a PR number\n- **THEN** the skill fetches the PR diff with `gh pr diff <number>` before spawning reviewers\n\n#### Scenario: File path argument reviews that file\n- **WHEN** `/adversarial <path>` is invoked with a file path\n- **THEN** the skill reads the specified file and uses it as the review target\n\n### Requirement: Two agents run concurrently\nThe skill SHALL spawn a Codex reviewer and a Claude reviewer in parallel so both complete in approximately the same wall time as the slower reviewer.\n\n#### Scenario: Codex reviewer dispatched async first\n- **WHEN** `/adversarial` executes\n- **THEN** the Codex reviewer is dispatched via `darkfactory-dispatch --async` before the Claude reviewer is launched\n- **AND** the Claude reviewer is launched via the Agent tool after the Codex dispatch returns a job ID\n\n#### Scenario: Both reviewers receive identical input\n- **WHEN** both reviewers are spawned\n- **THEN** each receives the same review target content (diff or file)\n- **AND** each receives the same review instructions\n\n### Requirement: Reviewer prompts are adversarial and independent\nEach reviewer SHALL be instructed to review independently, without seeing the other's output.\n\n#### Scenario: Adversarial framing in prompts\n- **WHEN** each reviewer's prompt is inspected\n- **THEN** it instructs the reviewer to be independent and opinionated\n- **AND** it does not include the other reviewer's output or conclusions\n\n### Requirement: Findings grouped by severity\nEach reviewer's output SHALL group findings into severity levels.\n\n#### Scenario: Severity levels present\n- **WHEN** a reviewer produces output\n- **THEN** findings are grouped as: critical, warning, nit\n- **AND** each finding includes a `file:line` reference where applicable\n\n### Requirement: Reports written to files\nBoth reviewer reports SHALL be written to the local filesystem.\n\n#### Scenario: Codex report file\n- **WHEN** `/adversarial` completes\n- **THEN** the Codex reviewer's report is written to `mission/validations/adversarial-codex.md` (or a temp path if run outside a mission)\n\n#### Scenario: Claude report file\n- **WHEN** `/adversarial` completes\n- **THEN** the Claude reviewer's report is written to `mission/validations/adversarial-claude.md` (or a temp path if run outside a mission)\n\n### Requirement: Disagreements surfaced\nAfter both reports are collected, the skill SHALL identify and surface points where the two reviewers disagree.\n\n#### Scenario: Disagreements highlighted in summary\n- **WHEN** both reviewer reports are collected\n- **THEN** the skill presents a synthesis to the human that calls out findings mentioned by one reviewer but not the other, or findings where the severity assessment differs\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"tool_end","dispatch_id":"01KQ7GQ976BYM3RDS75E2VS1QQ","ts":"2026-04-27T13:06:11Z","tool":"command_execution"}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' openspec/changes/skill-decomposition/specs/install-script/spec.md\"","aggregated_output":"## ADDED Requirements\n\n### Requirement: install.sh exists at repo root\nA POSIX-compatible shell script named `install.sh` SHALL exist at `~/.darkfactory/install.sh` and be executable.\n\n#### Scenario: Script is present and executable\n- **WHEN** a developer clones the Darkfactory repo\n- **THEN** `~/.darkfactory/install.sh` exists\n- **AND** the file is executable (`test -x ~/.darkfactory/install.sh` returns 0)\n- **AND** the script's shebang is `#!/bin/sh` (not `#!/bin/bash`)\n\n### Requirement: install.sh creates symlinks for all 12 skills\nRunning `install.sh` SHALL create a symlink in `~/.claude/skills/<name>` pointing to `~/.darkfactory/skills/<name>` for each of the 12 skills.\n\n#### Scenario: All 12 skill symlinks created\n- **WHEN** `~/.darkfactory/install.sh` is run on a clean machine (no existing symlinks)\n- **THEN** the following symlinks are created: `~/.claude/skills/mission`, `~/.claude/skills/grill`, `~/.claude/skills/language`, `~/.claude/skills/prd`, `~/.claude/skills/adversarial`, `~/.claude/skills/dispatch`, `~/.claude/skills/tdd`, `~/.claude/skills/test-quality`, `~/.claude/skills/security`, `~/.claude/skills/mission-resume`, `~/.claude/skills/mission-status`, `~/.claude/skills/mission-init`\n- **AND** each symlink resolves to its corresponding `~/.darkfactory/skills/<name>` directory\n\n### Requirement: install.sh is idempotent\nRunning `install.sh` a second time SHALL produce the same result without errors.\n\n#### Scenario: Re-run on existing symlinks\n- **WHEN** `~/.darkfactory/install.sh` is run after it has already been run\n- **THEN** the script exits with code 0\n- **AND** all 12 symlinks still resolve correctly\n- **AND** no existing non-Darkfactory skills in `~/.claude/skills/` are modified or removed\n\n### Requirement: install.sh works on macOS and Linux\nThe script SHALL use only POSIX-portable constructs and work on both macOS (BSD coreutils) and Debian/Ubuntu (GNU coreutils).\n\n#### Scenario: Script uses no GNU-only flags\n- **WHEN** `install.sh` is reviewed\n- **THEN** it contains no `sed -i`, `date -d`, `stat -c`, `mktemp --suffix`, `readlink -f`, or `grep -P` calls\n- **AND** `ln -sf` is used to create symlinks (handles both creating and updating)\n\n### Requirement: install.sh reports what it did\nAfter running, the script SHALL print a summary of what was linked.\n\n#### Scenario: Successful install output\n- **WHEN** `~/.darkfactory/install.sh` runs successfully\n- **THEN** it prints one line per skill symlink created or already-present\n- **AND** the final line reports the total number of skills installed\n- **AND** it exits with code 0\n\n### Requirement: README reflects the new install process and skill set\nThe README.md SHALL be updated to match the post-refactor structure.\n\n#### Scenario: Setup section replaced with install.sh\n- **WHEN** README.md is inspected\n- **THEN** the \"First-time install\" section shows `~/.darkfactory/install.sh` as the single install command\n- **AND** it contains no manual `ln -sf` commands for individual skills\n\n#### Scenario: Skills table uses current names\n- **WHEN** the README.md skills table is inspected\n- **THEN** it lists skills under their current names (e.g. `/mission-init`, `/mission-resume`, `/mission-status`)\n- **AND** it contains no legacy names (`/darkfactory-init`)\n\n#### Scenario: Required external skills section removed or updated\n- **WHEN** README.md is inspected\n- **THEN** the skills previously listed as \"required external\" from `layercodedev/skills` (`/grill-me`, `/ubiquitous-language`, `/write-a-prd`, `/tdd`, `/security-review`, `/test-quality-review`) are no longer described as external\n- **AND** they are either listed in the owned skills table or described as bundled\n- **AND** the only skills still marked as optional/project-specific are `/test-app` and `/demo-video`\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"tool_end","dispatch_id":"01KQ7GQ976BYM3RDS75E2VS1QQ","ts":"2026-04-27T13:06:11Z","tool":"command_execution"}
